    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc6-dxwl",
      "title": "specs: Add L2 Contract Upgrades Specification (Part 1)",
      "author": "maurelian",
      "number": 874,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nThis PR adds the first part of the L2 Contract Upgrades specification, converting the design doc into a formal spec that follows the established patterns in `specs/experimental/contracts/`.\r\n\r\n## Components Specified\r\n\r\nThis PR includes specifications for the first 3 of 6 components:\r\n\r\n1. ✅ **ConditionalDeployer** - Deterministic contract deployment with collision detection\r\n2. ✅ **L2ProxyAdmin (Upgraded)** - Enhanced proxy admin with `upgradePredeploys()` capability  \r\n3. ✅ **L2ContractsManager** - Configuration gathering and upgrade execution logic\r\n4. ⏳ Network Upgrade Transaction (NUT) Bundle - Format, generation, and execution requirements\r\n5. ⏳ Custom upgrade block gas limit - Mechanism for guaranteeing sufficient gas\r\n6. ⏳ Upgrade Process - End-to-end upgrade flow and sequencing requirements\r\n\r\n## Specification Structure\r\n\r\nEach component includes:\r\n- **Overview** - Purpose and role of the component\r\n- **Definitions** - Key terms with cross-references\r\n- **Assumptions** - External dependencies with mitigations\r\n- **Invariants** - Critical properties that must hold, with severity ratings\r\n- **Function Specification** - Detailed behavior using RFC 2119 keywords\r\n\r\n## Next Steps\r\n\r\nRemaining components (4-6) will be added in follow-up PRs to keep review scope manageable.\r\n\r\n## Related\r\n\r\n- [Design doc](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/design-docs/blob/3074f0ee0e809ca12ae2358e76aed8f58d9a8c50/protocol/l2-contract-upgrades.md#L1)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-21T14:26:50Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 517,
      "deletions": 0
    },
